There's no reason to use h; you'll get out faster if you go diagonally.
 I'd go e.g. northwest just to climb out--once you get the "you crawl
to the edge of the pit" message you can go west or wherever.

I'd definitely use the /slow monster; otherwise, once you get out the
roving leocratta is much faster than you.  It will be much easier to
outrun it and find the upstairs once you have slowed it down (the
slowness is permanent), and you're a lot safer slowing it down before
stepping off your E-square than after.  Just make sure you have
successfully written Elbereth before trying the wand (double-check with
the : key).

Also, once the q is slow then you have more turns to climb out when its
2+ squares away.  It does take longer to flee but you know you have
more time once it's out at that range.

